# A böngészős tesztkészlet 2026-08-04-én kikerült a repóból (BL-43), a maradék könyvtárai
# 2026-08-06-án. A node_modules/ és a futás közben keletkező mappák szabályai maradnak: a
# fejlesztői gépeken ott vannak, és soha nem is tartoztak ide.
/screens/
/node_modules/
# macOS Finder metadata - never useful in the repo.
**/.DS_Store
# Word/LibreOffice owner files. These are 162-byte temporary files that exist only while a document
# is open, and they are named after the document with a "~$" prefix - so they appear next to every
# .docx in docs/ the moment anyone opens one. Two of them reached the history on 2026-08-03 through
# a `git add -A`, which is exactly the accident this line prevents.
**/~$*
.~lock.*#

# Marketing képanyag. Nem a plugin része: semmi nem hivatkozik rá a kódból, nem olvassa a plugin, és
# a csomagba sem való. 2026-08-05-én 2,2 MB-nyi kép került be innen két commitba egy `git add -A`
# miatt - ugyanaz a baleset, ami a ~$* szabályt is kikényszerítette két nappal korábban. A fájlok a
# lemezen maradnak, csak a verziókövetésből kerülnek ki.
/assets/

# Never commit signed license files or private/signing keys. The dev .lic is generated
# on demand (see the runbook §5) and lives only under tools/ transiently; the RSA private
# key stays outside the repo entirely.
*.lic
*.pem
# Exception: the small signed .lic fixtures the PHPUnit license tests read (no secrets - they
# are signed with the dev key and carry no file-integrity manifest).
!tests/fixtures/licenses/*.lic

# Working documents left the repository on 2026-07-30, and the product documents followed them on
# 2026-08-04 (BL-45). Both now live in
# ~/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/moodle_dev_projektek/artqtml-munkadokumentumok/
# - the product ones under termekdokumentumok/. Plugin-agnostic checklists live in
# moodle_dev_projektek/general/. None of them is read by the plugin, shipped in the package or used
# by CI, and keeping them here produced commit noise plus a second place for decisions to drift into.
#
# The seven /docs/... rules that used to sit here are gone with the folder. They are not needed as
# a safety net: `docs/` is not a path this repository has any more, so nothing can land in it by
# accident. If a `docs/` folder ever comes back, it comes back on purpose and brings its own rules.
/result.md

# Generated by Moodle on every PHPUnit init (lib/phpunit/classes/util.php,
# build_component_config_files()), so committing it would dirty the tree on every run.
/phpunit.xml

# Written by tools/gates.sh on every run: the full output of the three gates, so the result can be
# read from the file instead of copied out of a terminal. Machine-local and rewritten each time,
# so it has no business in the history. The stamp file next to it records which plugin version the
# PHPUnit environment was last initialised for.
/tools/.gates-last.txt
/tools/.phpunit-initialised-at

# Ugyanez tools/cron.sh-ra: a sorban álló generálások végigfuttatásának teljes kimenete.
/tools/.cron-last.txt

# Composer vendor for the local/CI PHPStan toolchain (tools/devtools). Manifest is tracked;
# packages are installed on demand (see tools/TOOLCHAIN.md).
/tools/devtools/vendor/
/tools/devtools/composer.lock

# Personal Claude Code tool permissions, with absolute paths to this machine. The shared
# .claude/skills/ tree stays tracked.
/.claude/settings.local.json
